What is Tiny Core Linux?
Tiny Core Linux is a highly minimalist, ultra-lightweight Linux distribution. Instead of being a fully loaded operating system out of the box, it provides only the bare minimum required to boot into a very basic graphical user interface (GUI).
The Size: While a standard operating system like Ubuntu or Windows takes up 5 GB to 20 GB, Tiny Core is only about 11 MB to 23 MB in size.
How it works: It boots and runs entirely inside your computer's RAM. This makes it incredibly fast, but also means that by default, any changes you make vanish when you reboot, unless you explicitly configure persistent storage.
